  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Object-level propositions (evaluated per object)",
      "items": [
        "identity \u2014 a stable identifier pins this object. Not its contents.",
        "precedence \u2014 committed before the execution seal naming it. Not consumption.",
        "witness_attestation \u2014 an outside key signed its capture. Not that the witness is independent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Execution and assignment level",
      "items": [
        "recipe_available \u2014 a version-pinned reproduction path exists. Not that it ran.",
        "recipe_reproduced \u2014 a verifier reproduced the output. Not historical occurrence.",
        "historical_execution_established \u2014 only via observed-execution witness. Never inferred.",
        "external_time_bounds \u2014 the physical window. Not the content.",
        "assignment_disclosure \u2014 short disclosure within the custodian-held set. Not completeness of the world."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Non-implication rule",
      "items": [
        "No property upgrades another. No object inherits another's verdict.",
        "Reproduction does not prove historical execution.",
        "A valid chain does not prove the disclosed set is whole.",
        "input.precedence does not establish configuration.precedence.",
        "Verdicts: ESTABLISHED, UNESTABLISHED, UNCHECKED, UNAVAILABLE. None is a weak pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The wedge, and its likely first verdict",
      "items": [
        "Configuration sits with the provider and is overwritten on revision.",
        "The lender cannot timestamp what it does not hold.",
        "Likely first integration: configuration.identity ESTABLISHED, precedence and witness UNAVAILABLE.",
        "That is weaker than the wedge needs. It depends on provider cooperation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Claim status, distinct from build status",
      "items": [
        "FACT \u2014 a real execution-evidence problem exists.",
        "FACT \u2014 workflows exist where the operator cannot reconstruct execution state.",
        "THESIS \u2014 independent custody establishes more than logging or timestamping.",
        "HYPOTHESIS \u2014 a party bearing the loss will pay in advance to preserve it.",
        "UNKNOWN \u2014 whether any provider will expose a configuration digest at execution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Open, and named rather than hidden",
      "items": [
        "Capture at execution time is not implemented.",
        "Boundary establishment: nothing prevents execution outside the instrumented path.",
        "Who the witness is, and whether anyone checks what they signed.",
        "Money is spent because this evidence is absent. Established.",
        "That spend converts into a pre-loss purchase. Untested."
      ]
    }
  ]
